  "overview": "Replace the cron with retries that live in the broker (delayed publish), record when a delivery gives up, and build the smallest operator surface that makes those deliveries visible. Alerts are optional and depend on decision 2.",
  "sections": [
   {
    "id": "retry",
    "title": "Retry scheduler",
    "mechanical": false,
    "summary": "New `internal/retry` package: a backoff policy plus a scheduler that publishes delayed copies to the delivery queue.",
    "blocks": [
     {
      "type": "markdown",
      "md": "Options considered:\n\n1. **Broker delayed publish** (chosen): no new storage, survives restarts.\n2. A `retries` table polled every few seconds: more moving parts, a hot table.\n3. Keep the cron, add backoff: still races with the consumer.",
      "id": "retry-1",
      "level": 2
     },
     {
      "type": "steps",
      "steps": [
       {
        "title": "Policy with Delay(attempt)",
        "detail": "Capped exponential, full jitter. Unit-test the cap and exhaustion.",
        "status": "todo"
       },
       {
        "title": "Scheduler.Schedule / Replay",
        "detail": "Thin wrapper over `PublishAt`.",
        "status": "todo"
       },
       {
        "title": "Bump amqp091-go for x-delay support",
        "status": "todo"
       }
      ],
      "id": "retry-2",
      "level": 2
     },
     {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "go",
      "file": "internal/retry/scheduler.go (sketch)",
      "code": "type Scheduler struct {\n\tqueue  deliverymq.Publisher\n\tpolicy Policy\n}\n\nfunc (s *Scheduler) Schedule(ctx context.Context, d models.Delivery) (Outcome, error)\nfunc (s *Scheduler) Replay(ctx context.Context, d models.Delivery) error\n",
      "id": "retry-3",
      "level": 3
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "consumer",
    "title": "Consumer: schedule, then ack",
    "mechanical": false,
    "summary": "On failure the consumer calls the scheduler and acks the original only once the retry is queued.",
    "blocks": [
     {
      "type": "flow",
      "mermaid": "flowchart LR\n  A[deliver] --> B{2xx?}\n  B -- yes --> C[ack]\n  B -- no --> D[Schedule retry]\n  D -- queued --> C\n  D -- exhausted --> E[MarkFailed] --> C\n  D -- error --> F[nack]",
      "id": "consumer-1",
      "level": 2
     },
     {
      "type": "callout",
      "tone": "risk",
      "md": "Never ack before the retry is queued: that order drops events on a crash.",
      "id": "consumer-2",
      "level": 2
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "schema",
    "title": "Schema: record failures",
    "mechanical": false,
    "summary": "Add `next_attempt_at` and `failed_at` to `delivery_attempts`, plus a partial index for the operator list.",
    "blocks": [
     {
      "type": "data-model",
      "entities": [
       {
        "name": "delivery_attempts",
        "change": "changed",
        "fields": [
